  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response to deliver lifesaving assistance to the Ukrainian refugees in Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to support the refugee response organised by the authorities, HelpAge will be providing these refugee collective centres with food support and NFIs, to ensure that the basic food, hygiene and basic items needs of the Ukrainian refugees are met. Food support will be provided as a combination of food items for those centres that have kitchen facilities and provide with meals themselves, and delivery of hot meals to those centres that do now have their own system for food preparation. In terms of hygiene and basic items delivery, these will be given to each person once a month. The hygiene kits can contain toothbrush adult size, toothpaste, soap bars, shampoo, adult diapers, gel, toilet paper, garbage bags, medical masks, rubber gloves, disposable razor, towel and hand antiseptic. The emergency kits can include blankets, candles, matches, water containers, cooking utensils, batteries and torches.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide emergency NFI and hygiene kits to the Ukrainian refugees staying in Refugee collective centers in Moldova</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide lifesaving humanitarian food assistance to the Ukrainian refugees staying in Refugee collective centers in Moldova</narrative>
  </description>
